    "body": "fix on issue/2475-wcs-flip-mill-posts · PR #2749 · pinned by a_flipped_wcs_cuts_the_cam_path_in_each_mill_dialect, an_inverted_machine_axis_cuts_the_cam_path_in_each_mill_dialect, radius_word_arcs_follow_the_mirror, each_dialect_names_the_flipped_axes_and_the_inverted_axes, a_plain_section_after_a_flipped_one_writes_no_flip_note, probing_on_an_inverted_axis_stays_refused_in_the_new_dialects, flipped_x_goldens_for_the_new_dialects · merges when reviewed\n\nResult for each script: Mazak, Doosan DNM, Siemens 840D, Heidenhain, Mach4, grblHAL, Tormach, TinyG, Carvera and LinuxCNC declare `axisInversion = true`. The trace of each is on the CAM path for a flipped X, Y, and X and Y. No script has a recorded reason why it cannot. Probing stays refused.\n\nOne line is stale after this PR: `.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md` says \"Fanuc and Haas are\" for `set_wcs_flip`. The worker session could not write to `.claude/skills`.\n",
